  "articleBody": "Trim takes the brunt of household wear, pet activity, and outdoor weather exposure. Deciding whether to repair an isolated patch or replace full lengths helps you protect underlying framing without overspending.\n\nKey Benefits\nAddressing damaged trim promptly preserves structural building materials beneath walls and windows. Timely work also stops water penetration before it causes framing rot or drywall deterioration.\n\nProcess Breakdown\nThe technician begins by identifying the root cause of damage, such as a plumbing leak, pets, or exterior weather exposure. Rotted or soft material is completely cut away back to clean, sound substrate. After allowing any damp wood to dry thoroughly (which can take 24 to 48 hours in exterior spots), the contractor measures the profile, cuts matching stock, secures it, seals the seams, and finishes the surface with primer and paint.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options\nIsolated dents or minor surface cracks usually only need wood filler and repainting. However, when wood has gone soft, cracked across full spans, or suffered recurring water exposure, full section replacement is the only reliable fix.\n\nGetting Started\nMake sure your estimate covers disposal, profile matching, and finishing paint. HH Remodeling LLC provides complete repair and handyman solutions across Aurora and the Denver metro. For an honest evaluation of your home's trim, contact Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
